px;max-width:250px;"><svg viewBox="0 0 220 236" role="img" aria-label="Adding chroma gives a third axis: hue rotates, lightness rises, chroma runs outward" style="width:100%;height:auto;display:block;"><defs><marker id="dgmArrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 z" fill="var(--fg)"/></marker></defs><ellipse cx="110" cy="148" rx="72" ry="23" fill="none" stroke="var(--rule)" stroke-width="1"/><line x1="110" y1="152" x2="110" y2="30" stroke="var(--fg)" stroke-width="1.3" marker-end="url(#dgmArrow)"/><line x1="110" y1="148" x2="176" y2="158" stroke="var(--fg)" stroke-width="1.3" marker-end="url(#dgmArrow)"/><path d="M44 140A72 23 0 0 1 148 131" fill="none" stroke="var(--fg)" stroke-width="1.3" marker-end="url(#dgmArrow)"/><circle cx="110" cy="148" r="3" fill="var(--fg)"/><text x="118" y="38" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--fg)">lightness</text><text x="128" y="178" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--fg)">chroma</text><text x="96" y="120" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--fg)">hue</text><text x="110" y="208" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12.5" font-weight="500" fill="var(--fg)">3 &mdash; + chroma</text><text x="110" y="226" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" fill="var(--muted)">a solid &mdash; and not a tidy one</text></svg></div></div><div style="margin-top:1.6rem;max-width:520px;"><svg viewBox="0 0 420 356" role="img" aria-label="Measured cross-section of the sRGB gamut in CIELAB at the yellow and blue hue planes" style="width:100%;height:auto;display:block;"><defs><linearGradient id="dgmNeutral" x1="0" y1="1" x2="0" y2="0"><stop offset="0" stop-color="#000000"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#FFFFFF"/></linearGradient><linearGradient id="dgmYel" x1="0" y1="1" x2="0" y2="0"><stop offset="0" stop-color="#241F00"/><stop offset=".5" stop-color="#A89B00"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#FFFF33"/></linearGradient><linearGradient id="dgmBlu" x1="0" y1="1" x2="0" y2="0"><stop offset="0" stop-color="#07001F"/><stop offset=".32" stop-color="#1A0DF2"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#D4CFFF"/></linearGradient></defs><line x1="38" y1="300" x2="402" y2="300" stroke="var(--rule-soft)" stroke-width="1"/><line x1="38" y1="240" x2="402" y2="240" stroke="var(--rule-soft)" stroke-width="1"/><line x1="38" y1="180" x2="402" y2="180" stroke="var(--rule-soft)" stroke-width="1"/><line x1="38" y1="120" x2="402" y2="120" stroke="var(--rule-soft)" stroke-width="1"/><line x1="38" y1="60" x2="402" y2="60" stroke="var(--rule-soft)" stroke-width="1"/><path d="M216 300L216 300L162.9 290.4L151.2 280.8L141.39 271.2L131.22 261.6L121.41 252L111.87 242.4L101.34 232.8L95.58 223.2L97.47 213.6L102.69 204L110.7 194.4L118.62 184.8L126.27 175.2L133.47 165.6L141.75 156L148.41 146.4L155.97 136.8L163.53 127.2L171 117.6L177.66 108L185.13 98.4L192.42 88.8L199.71 79.2L205.92 69.6L216 60Z" fill="url(#dgmBlu)" stroke="var(--rule)" stroke-width=".8"/><path d="M216 300L216 300L223.92 290.4L229.05 280.8L234.81 271.2L239.22 261.6L243.9 252L247.95 242.4L251.46 232.8L254.61 223.2L257.58 213.6L260.55 204L263.97 194.4L266.85 184.8L270.09 175.2L273.33 165.6L276.57 156L279.27 146.4L282.33 136.8L285.48 127.2L288.99 117.6L291.96 108L294.93 98.4L298.35 88.8L301.23 79.2L303.3 69.6L303.21 66.96L216 60Z" fill="url(#dgmYel)" stroke="var(--rule)" stroke-width=".8"/><rect x="212" y="60" width="8" height="240" fill="url(#dgmNeutral)" stroke="var(--rule)" stroke-width=".8"/><text x="8" y="44" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--muted)">L*</text><text x="8" y="300" dominant-baseline="middle" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--muted)">0</text><text x="8" y="240" dominant-baseline="middle" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--muted)">25</text><text x="8" y="180" dominant-baseline="middle" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--muted)">50</text><text x="8" y="120" dominant-baseline="middle" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--muted)">75</text><text x="8" y="60" dominant-baseline="middle" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--muted)">100</text><text x="216" y="50" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" fill="var(--fg)">white</text><text x="216" y="316" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" fill="var(--fg)">black</text><circle cx="303.21" cy="69.6" r="3.6" fill="none" stroke="var(--fg)" stroke-width="1.4"/><line x1="307.21" y1="69.6" x2="310" y2="69.6" stroke="var(--fg)" stroke-width="1"/><text x="313" y="66.6" font-size="11.5" font-weight="500" fill="var(--fg)">yellow peaks light</text><text x="313" y="81.6" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--muted)">L* 97, C* 97</text><circle cx="95.58" cy="223.2" r="3.6" fill="none" stroke="var(--fg)" stroke-width="1.4"/><line x1="92.58" y1="226.2" x2="62" y2="262" stroke="var(--fg)" stroke-width="1"/><text x="6" y="274" font-size="11.5" font-weight="500" fill="var(--fg)">blue peaks dark</text><text x="6" y="288" font-size="10.5" fill="var(--muted)">L* 32, C* 134</text><text x="120" y="340" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" fill="var(--muted)">&#8592; chroma &middot; blue plane</text><text x="312" y="340" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" fill="var(--muted)">chroma &middot; yellow plane &#8594;</text></svg></div><figcaption style="margin-top:.7rem;font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.55;color:var(--muted);">A wheel carries one coordinate; a colour solid carries three, and the third is what makes it lumpy. The lower figure is <b>not</b> a picture of the Munsell solid and not a 3D render of anything &mdash; it is a measured cross-section of the <b>sRGB</b> gamut, computed by sampling the surface of the sRGB cube and converting to CIELAB (D65, 2&deg; observer). Each wing plots the greatest chroma reachable at that lightness on one hue plane: yellow (h<sub>ab</sub> 103&deg;) to the right, blue (h<sub>ab</sub> 306&deg;) to the left; the endpoints are pinned to zero chroma at black and white, which is exact. The asymmetry is the whole point &mdash; the most saturated yellow sits at L* 97, almost at white, while the most saturated blue sits at L* 32, well down toward black. Maximum chroma is a different number at every hue and every lightness, so no regular shape &mdash; sphere, cylinder or double cone &mdash; can be the true solid. Munsell&rsquo;s solid is irregular for the same reason, measured from pigments rather than computed from a screen gamut.</figcaption></figure>
